<%# The owner flash. #flash-messages must exist on every render, empty or not —
    owner/wine_list_items replaces it by id from a Turbo Stream, and a missing
    target is a silently dropped message. It is the Turbo target and nothing
    else: no styling, no fixed positioning of its own, so when there is no
    flash it is an empty div that occupies no height.

    The stack inside it is the same one the public shell renders — see
    shared/_flash_band — but unlike the public one it is rendered
    unconditionally, because it is not only the flash's home any more. Arriving
    orders are appended to it by the poller (owner/orders/notifications), and a
    stack that only exists when there happens to be a flash is a stack the first
    order of the evening lands beside rather than in. It costs nothing when
    empty: the stack is fixed, so it is out of flow, and pointer-events: none,
    so it is not a dead zone over the corner of the page.

    data-turbo-temporary on the stack, not on the wrapper. Turbo caches the page
    as it leaves it and paints that snapshot instantly on back/forward before
    the fresh fetch arrives; a message baked into the snapshot is one the reader
    already dealt with, and it does not come back quietly — it slides in and
    arms a fresh timer, so it reads as something new having just happened. That
    is as true of an order announced ten minutes ago as of a flash. The wrapper
    has to survive into the snapshot for the opposite reason: it is the Turbo
    Stream target, and a stream that lands on a restored page with no
    #flash-messages in it drops the message silently. %>
<div id="flash-messages">
  <div class="toast-stack" data-turbo-temporary id="owner-toast-stack">
    <% if notice %>
      <%= render "shared/flash_band",
                 variant: "alert-success",
                 icon_name: "check-circle",
                 label: t("shared.flash_notice"),
                 message: notice %>
    <% end %>
    <% if alert %>
      <%= render "shared/flash_band",
                 variant: "alert-error",
                 icon_name: "warning",
                 label: t("shared.flash_error"),
                 message: alert %>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
